		{"id":"discussion","type":"text","text":"## Discussion Pivots\n\n1. What is your practice *thinking* right now?\n2. What's a recurring hassle (friction) in your workflow?\n3. What does your primary tool amplify? What does it reduce?\n4. Where do you feel the split between doing and thinking?\n5. What would it mean to learn your tools on *their* terms?","x":-700,"y":400,"width":560,"height":300,"color":"2"},
		{"id":"asn_hook","type":"text","text":"## ASN 1: Potluck + Reading Propositions\n\nDue Week 2.\n\n- Read Manning & Massumi, *Thought in the Act* (selections — see Reading Guide)\n- Bring one object to the **(Im)material Potluck**: something from your practice that is both material and immaterial, or that troubles that distinction\n- Be prepared to describe: what it does, what it thinks, what it can't say","x":90,"y":400,"width":500,"height":300,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"subA","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 01 - Practice Immanent Critique/submodules/DIGM 553 - W01A - Research-Creation as Method.md","x":-940,"y":-80,"width":420,"height":280},
		{"id":"subB","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Week 01 - Practice Immanent Critique/submodules/DIGM 553 - W01B - Epistemic Tools Introduction.md","x":-270,"y":-80,"width":420,"height":280},
		{"id":"read_agre","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Notes - FOR INSTRUCTOR ONLY/reading-guides/Agre — Critical Technical Practice.md","x":640,"y":-700,"width":340,"height":440,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"opening","type":"text","text":"# Opening Provocation\n\n*\"Every practice is a mode of thought, already in the act. To dance: a thinking in movement. To paint: a thinking through color.\"*\n— Manning & Massumi\n\n**What is your current practice thinking?**","x":-400,"y":-1640,"width":680,"height":200,"color":"6"},
		{"id":"read_manning","type":"file","file":"DIGM 553/Notes - FOR INSTRUCTOR ONLY/reading-guides/Manning + Massumi — Thought in the Act.md","x":-1110,"y":-700,"width":340,"height":440,"color":"4"},
